   # ESP32-S3 MASTER HARDWARE & PINOUT MAP
========================================================================================================================
Target: Espressif ESP32-S3 (WROOM-1, WROOM-2, Mini, DevKitC-1)
Rule #1: GPIO 22, 23, 24, and 25 DO NOT EXIST in the silicon die.
Rule #2: ESP32-S3 has NO DAC (0 channels).
Rule #3: ESP32-S3 has NO INPUT-ONLY pins (All 45 GPIOs are bidirectional with pull-up/pull-down).
========================================================================================================================

------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
[SECTION 1] HARDWARE SUBSYSTEM CAPABILITIES & CONFLICT RULES
------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
PERIPHERAL      | CAPACITY            | KEY CONFLICTS & HARDWARE RULES
----------------+---------------------+---------------------------------------------------------------------------------
DAC             | 0 Channels (NONE)   | No DAC hardware. Use LEDC (PWM) + RC Filter, or external I2S DAC (MAX98357A).
ADC1            | 10 Channels (12-bit)| GPIO 1 to 10 (ADC1_CH0 - CH9). Completely safe to use with Wi-Fi / Bluetooth.
ADC2            | 10 Channels (12-bit)| GPIO 11 to 20 (ADC2_CH0 - CH9). CONFLICTS WITH WI-FI! Avoid if Wi-Fi is active.
Touch Sensor    | 14 Channels         | GPIO 1 to 14 map 1:1 to TOUCH 1 to 14.
RTC GPIO        | 22 Channels         | GPIO 0 to 21 map 1:1 to RTC_GPIO 0 to 21. Wakeup from Deep Sleep & ULP monitor.
Interrupts      | All 45 GPIOs        | All usable GPIOs support Edge/Level external interrupts.
PWM (LEDC)      | 8 Channels (1-14b)  | Can be routed to ANY valid output GPIO via GPIO Matrix.
PWM (MCPWM)     | 2 Groups (6 outputs)| Motor control PWM; can be routed to ANY valid output GPIO via GPIO Matrix.
I2C (0 & 1)     | 2 Controllers       | Route to ANY GPIO via Matrix. Typical: SDA=GPIO 8, SCL=GPIO 9.
SPI (SPI2/FSPI) | 1 User Controller   | Native pins (<=80MHz): CS=10, MOSI=11, SCK=12, MISO=13. Any pin via Matrix (<=40MHz).
Native USB      | USB OTG / Serial    | GPIO 19 (D-) and GPIO 20 (D+). Reserved if using native USB-CDC/JTAG port.
UART0 (Console) | Boot / Flash port   | GPIO 43 (TX) and GPIO 44 (RX). Routed to onboard CP2102/CH340 chip on devkits.
UART1           | Secondary UART      | Native IO_MUX: TX=GPIO 17, RX=GPIO 18. (Can also be routed to any GPIO).
UART2           | Tertiary UART       | No direct IO_MUX pins. Routable to ANY GPIO via GPIO Matrix.

