------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
[SECTION 3] BOOT STRAPPING PINS (RESET CRITICAL RULES)
------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
PIN      | DEFAULT STATE     | FUNCTIONALITY & RISK
---------+-------------------+------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
GPIO 0   | Pull-UP (1)       | Boot Mode: 1 = SPI Boot (Normal Run), 0 = Download Mode (Flashing).
         |                   | External button to GND is fine. Do not pull LOW permanently!
---------+-------------------+------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
GPIO 45  | Pull-DOWN (0)     | SPI Flash Voltage (VDD_SPI): 0 = 3.3V rail, 1 = 1.8V rail.
         |                   | EXTREME DANGER: Never pull HIGH externally on standard 3.3V flash modules!
---------+-------------------+------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
GPIO 46  | Pull-DOWN (0)     | Boot Diagnostic Print: 0 = Print ROM logs, 1 = Clean boot / muted logs.
         |                   | DANGER: If GPIO 0 is LOW and GPIO 46 is HIGH, SoC enters an INVALID boot state.
---------+-------------------+------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
GPIO 3   | Floating          | JTAG Signal Selection: Controls whether JTAG routes to USB-JTAG or GPIOs 39-42.
         |                   | Keep floating or use a weak pull-down. Do not tie hard to 3.3V.

